        prompts: {
          human: 'Tàihé A Bāo (泰和A包) is a Chinese climbing game from Taihe county, Jiangxi province. Four players: one declarer vs the other three each hand. 40-card deck (remove 2s, 3s, 8s); rank A, K, Q, J, 10, 9, 7, 6, 5, 4. Cards drawn from deck counterclockwise (not dealt). Bidding: declare or pass; if all pass, second round—call for a card (exchange); last caller is declarer. Play: declarer leads combinations; others beat or pass. Combinations: singles, pairs, sequences, double sequences, three-of-a-kind, four-of-a-kind (bombs beat any non-bomb). First out wins; if declarer wins they collect stakes from each opponent. Often played for money.',
          ai: 'Game: Tàihé A Bāo 泰和A包. Logic: First out wins; declarer wins or loses stakes per opponent based on bidding.',
